title: 'pallet-scheduler: remove aborted and unserviceable tasks from agendas'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Makes agenda servicing in `pallet-scheduler` more robust.

    Tasks aborted with `CallUnavailable` or `PermanentlyOverweight` are now removed from their
    agenda together with their name and retry configuration.

    A due task whose service weight exceeds `MaximumWeight` is now removed with
    `PermanentlyOverweight`. Tasks that fit `MaximumWeight` but not the weight left in the current
    block are still postponed.
    `MaximumWeight` should leave enough of the maximum block weight for the work done before the
    scheduler runs.

    The weight budget of a block is treated as fresh only until the first task is serviced.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    Scheduled tasks that fail with `CallUnavailable` or `PermanentlyOverweight` are removed from
    storage. Cancelling, rescheduling or setting a retry configuration for them by address now
    returns `NotFound`.

    Lowering the scheduler's `MaximumWeight` below a scheduled task removes that task when it is
    due. To pause the scheduler, set `MaximumWeight` to zero, which removes nothing.
crates:
- name: pallet-scheduler
  bump: patch
